.TH BUILDPKG 1 "September 2026" "Saphira Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
buildpkg \- request and run a native package build
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B buildpkg
.I PACKAGE
.RI [ SOURCE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B buildpkg
is the normal build frontend: it resolves the dependency closure
repository-first (see
.BR resolvepkg (1)),
assembles one disposable merged root for the top-level package, and
runs the recipe's
.BR recipe_build " and " recipe_install
(see
.BR recipe (5))
inside rootless containers. An explicit top-level request always
builds the current native recipe; dependencies are never rebuilt or
upgraded merely because a newer recipe exists.
.PP
There is no sudo and no root anywhere in the build path. One visible
workspace per top-level build appears at
.IR /build/PACKAGE.buildpkg .
A failed run retains its workspace as diagnostic evidence carrying
the marker content
.IR saphira-buildpkg-failed/v1 ;
retry requires that exact marker and unmarked collisions are refused.
Never delete, bless, or overwrite an unmarked workspace.
.SH OPTIONS
This command takes no options beyond the package name and optional
source override; build behavior comes from the recipe plus
configuration, not flags.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /build/PACKAGE.buildpkg
The evolving disposable root (merged view plus upper/work layers)
and retained logs/
.IR plan.json .
.TP
.I /build/rootfs_overlay/base
The canonical immutable base root all workspaces share.
.TP
.I /out/stage4/incoming/
Where successful builds land as unsigned
.I *-ready
transactions for publication (see
.BR sign-apk-repo (8)).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Built and staged successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Build failed; the workspace is retained with its failure marker for
diagnosis (see
.BR cleanpkg (1)
for the trusted removal lifecycle).
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS
buildpkg libxslt
.br
buildpkg nginx
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR recipe (5),
.BR saphira (7),
.BR resolvepkg (1),
.BR checkpkg (1),
.BR cleanpkg (1),
.BR sign-apk-repo (8),
.BR saphira-build (8)
